# Local secret / binary files that must never be committed.
#
# Deliberately matched by EXTENSION, never by name. A named entry here is a
# public index: this file is world-readable on a public repo, so naming a
# specific document tells a reader that document exists and is worth finding.
# One did name a credential-bearing file, which defeated an earlier redaction.
# Extension rules ignore strictly more and disclose nothing — keep it that way.
*.docx
*.doc
*.xlsx
*.xls
# Office lock/owner files
~$*
# Packaged VS Code extensions (e.g. clippar_app/kickbacks.vsix)
*.vsix
